WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.200
Why does this matter?

2
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.683
In this workbook's implementation guide,

3
00:00:03.683 --> 00:00:08.794
Gate 7 proves that one personnel action
changes access only through the attributes,

4
00:00:08.794 --> 00:00:11.788
with the mover workflow's
run history as evidence.

5
00:00:11.788 --> 00:00:15.316
Gate 8 puts leaver automation
first in every wave,

6
00:00:15.316 --> 00:00:18.587
and sizes Lifecycle
Workflows for the agency.

7
00:00:18.587 --> 00:00:20.850
The built-in tasks cover the account.

8
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:25.688
The rest of a leaver, such as the PIV
credential, the devices and the servers,

9
00:00:25.688 --> 00:00:29.575
goes through a custom task
extension that calls a Logic App.

10
00:00:29.575 --> 00:00:30.763
And here's the gap.

11
00:00:30.763 --> 00:00:35.769
The definition on Microsoft Learn's
page, Configure a Logic App for Lifecycle

12
00:00:35.769 --> 00:00:38.820
Workflow use, calls back
to the worldwide Graph,

13
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.324
on beta, and it always says it completed.

14
00:00:41.324 --> 00:00:45.600
In a GCC High tenant that
callback goes to the wrong cloud.

15
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.288
And a revocation that
failed reads as done.

16
00:00:48.288 --> 00:00:53.040
In this module you see what that costs,
and you run the definition that fixes it.
